{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"Graph","externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocols0A0P7CliquesE07maximalC0AD07MaximalC0VyxGyF","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"modules":[{"name":"Cliques","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Extended Protocol","symbolKind":"extension","role":"symbol"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/averageClustering()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cliqueNumber()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficient(of:)","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficients()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/coreNumbers()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/transitivity()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount(of:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumClique()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically least largest clique by vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. For each v, a witness clique W"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(any one of the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"candidate in W is taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the common neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least vertex of the best clique so far is skipped. Exponential in the worst case."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumClique"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","role":"symbol","title":"maximumClique()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumclique()"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount(of:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of triangles through "},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", from its neighborhood alone."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"triangleCount"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount(of:)","role":"symbol","title":"triangleCount(of:)","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/trianglecount(of:)"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/averageClustering()":{"title":"averageClustering()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/averageclustering()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/averageClustering()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"averageClustering","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The mean local clustering coefficient over every vertex, zeros included, summed in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; 0 when empty.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"title":"maximalCliques()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximalCliques"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MaximalCliques","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MaximalCliques"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/clusteringCoefficients()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Triangles and clustering for every vertex of the simple graph (self-loops ignored,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges counted once), in one compact-forward pass. O(m^(3\/2))."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clusteringCoefficients"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques22ClusteringCoefficientsV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ClusteringCoefficients"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficients()","role":"symbol","title":"clusteringCoefficients()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficients()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"title":"Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/transitivity()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Three times the triangles over the connected triples; 0 when there are no triangles.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transitivity"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"type":"topic","title":"transitivity()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/transitivity()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/transitivity()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/cliqueNumber()":{"title":"cliqueNumber()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/cliquenumber()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cliqueNumber()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cliqueNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The size of a largest clique of the simple graph, ω: 0 for the empty graph, 1 for an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edgeless one, at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracy + 1"},{"type":"text","text":". Branch and bound in degeneracy order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"each vertex’s later neighbors (at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"degeneracy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those with a high enough core number)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the candidates, one search per vertex that raises the best size as it goes, stopping at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the degeneracy bound. Each search is San Segundo et al.’s BBMC on bitsets, candidates in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"descending degree, branching from the highest greedy colour down. Exponential in the worst","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"case; memory O(n + m + degeneracy²).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount()":{"title":"triangleCount()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/trianglecount()","identifier":"do